  "body": "The `navigator.usb.test` API was written to provide a way to define the behavior of test devices so that the WebUSB API could be exercised without any real USB devices connected, such as in Web Platform Tests. This predates the development of the WebDriver BiDi specification. Bidirectional communication is required because test devices must react to input, rather than simply be configured with test values in the way that other APIs like Geolocation can be tested. The Web Bluetooth API has already completed this transition from a bespoke testing interface to a set of commands and events specified using WebDriver BiDi.\n\nThe test API specification will no longer be published when this specification is set up for publishing through the WHATWG deployment infrastructure because it does not support publishing multiple Bikeshed documents.",
